figdown 0.1 block
# spec §12.4 rule 4 and §12.6: `class=` is recorded as a REFERENCE and its
# presentation values are never copied onto the member. This case joins a
# class from every directive that accepts `class=` (§10 registry: node,
# group, edge, field, cell) — group/field/cell were previously unexercised
# — and the golden shows no fill, stroke or style on any member.
class hot "Hot path" fill=#fee2e2 stroke=#dc2626 style=dashed
group g "Group" class=hot
node a "A" in=g class=hot
node b "B" in=g
edge a -> b class=hot
bitfield bf "Bits" numbering=msb0
field "One" 4 class=hot
field "Two" 28
table t "Table"
| h | i |
|---|---|
| 1 | 2 |
cell (1,1) class=hot
